{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 formalization of two explicit, strictly increasing, pairwise disjoint infinite families x(m) and y(m) (m >= 0) of base-6 Lychrel numbers under repeated base-6 reverse-and-add T(n) = n + rev_6(n). Family 1 has 110 + 2m base-6 digits (smallest seed x(0) with 86 decimal digits) and Family 2 has 108 + 2m base-6 digits (smallest seed y(0) with 84 decimal digits), with middle blocks linked by base-6 digit complement d |-> 5 - d. Both satisfy the exact period-12 self-similar recurrence T^[12](x(m)) = x(m + 3) and T^[12](y(m)) = y(m + 3) while avoiding all base-6 palindromes, proving unconditionally that infinitely many base-6 Lychrel numbers exist.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Tyler B. Hughes"
    }
  ],
